  "knowledge": "Degradation-Adjusted Capacity",
  "description": "Estimates the current effective power capacity of a plant, accounting for cumulative performance degradation since it began operation.",
  "definition": "The plant's nameplate capacity adjusted for long-term wear and aging. The calculation is: $P_{adj} = P_{rated} \\times (1 - (\\text{Annual Degradation Rate} \\times \\text{Age}))$."
}

{
